#!/bin/sh
# Debian post-install script of ErgoPro2 (added by CPack, CMakeLists.txt).
# Prints the one-time setup note for Wayland sessions (B.1.4, BUILD.md 3).
set -e

if [ "$1" = "configure" ]; then
    cat <<'NOTE'

ErgoPro2 installed. Start it from the application menu ("ErgoPro2") or with: ErgoPro2

Wayland sessions only (Debian 13 GNOME default): global mouse/keyboard monitoring
reads /dev/input, so your user must be in the "input" group:

    sudo usermod -aG input "$USER"

then log out and log in again. X11 sessions need nothing.
Note: members of the "input" group can read all keyboard input of the machine.
See the user guide (documentation/USER_GUIDE.md) for details.

NOTE
fi

exit 0
